{"name":"Tree","description":"Expand and browse data with parent-child levels · A tree reveals folders, departments, categories, and other hierarchies by expanding and collapsing levels. It may support browsing, selection, or dragging. For permissions and selection, explain clearly how parent and child nodes affect each other.","quote":"Make it work like folders: click the little arrow to expand the next level.","agentPrompt":"Build the project browser as a tree: folders expand and collapse, files do not, indentation and icons expose levels, and expansion state persists. Test deep nesting, duplicate names, keyboard navigation, and narrow-screen indentation.","html":"<div class=\"detail-body detail-entry-tree\"><section class=\"detail-hero\" id=\"detail-hero\"><div class=\"dh-head\"><h1>Tree</h1></div><div class=\"dh-quote\"><span class=\"dh-quote-label\">You might say</span><p class=\"dh-quote-text\">Make it work like folders: click the little arrow to expand the next level.</p></div><div class=\"dh-tagline\"><strong class=\"dh-summary-lead\">Expand and browse data with parent-child levels</strong><span class=\"dh-summary-separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\">·</span><span>A tree reveals folders, departments, categories, and other hierarchies by expanding and collapsing levels. It may support browsing, selection, or dragging. For permissions and selection, explain clearly how parent and child nodes affect each other.</span></div><div class=\"dh-demo\"><div class=\"dh-demo-viewport\"><div class=\"dh-demo-inner\"><div class=\"tre-live\"><div class=\"tre-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"tre1\" checked><label class=\"tre-node\" for=\"tre1\"><span class=\"tre-arrow\">▸</span><span class=\"tre-label on\">Design Department</span></label><div class=\"tre-kids\"><div class=\"tre-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"tre2\"><label class=\"tre-node\" for=\"tre2\"><span class=\"tre-arrow\">▸</span><span class=\"tre-label\">UI group</span></label><div class=\"tre-kids\"><div class